Q21. Create a class Palindrome with a method using local variables to check if a number is palindrome. Add a class variable countChecks.

Program:

class Palindrome {
    static int countChecks = 0;

    void check(int n) {
        int temp = n, rev = 0;
        countChecks++;

        while (temp > 0) {
            rev = rev * 10 + temp % 10;
            temp /= 10;
        }

        System.out.println(n == rev ? "Palindrome" : "Not Palindrome");
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Palindrome p = new Palindrome();
        p.check(121);
        System.out.println("Checks = " + countChecks);
    }
}

